
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### ==================================================
### A. HEALTH CHECKS
### ==================================================

### A1. API health — should return 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### A2. Database health — should return 200 if connected
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/db


### ==================================================
### B. ORGANIZATION HEADER VALIDATION
### ==================================================

### B1. Missing organization header — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads

### B2. Non-numeric organization ID — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
x-org-id: abc

### B3. Zero organization ID — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
x-org-id: 0

### B4. Negative organization ID — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
x-org-id: -1

### B5. Decimal organization ID — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
x-org-id: 1.5

### B6. Valid organization ID — should pass header validation
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
x-org-id: 1


### ==================================================
### C. READ LEADS
### ==================================================

### C1. List leads for organization 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
x-org-id: 1

### C2. Filter leads by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads?status=contacted
x-org-id: 1

### C3. Invalid status — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads?status=pending
x-org-id: 1

### C4. Get lead ID 1 within organization 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/1
x-org-id: 1

### C5. Invalid lead ID — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/abc
x-org-id: 1

### C6. Nonexistent lead ID — should return 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/999999
x-org-id: 1


### ==================================================
### D. CREATE LEADS
### ==================================================

### D1. Create a lead for organization 1
# @name createOrg1Lead
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "name": "Day14 Test Lead",
  "email": "day14.test@example.com",
  "company": "Test Company",
  "phone": "9876543210"
}

### D2. Missing required field — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "name": "Missing Company",
  "email": "missing.company@example.com"
}

### D3. Invalid email — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "name": "Invalid Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "company": "Test Company"
}

### D4. Blank name — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "name": "   ",
  "email": "blank.name@example.com",
  "company": "Test Company"
}


### ==================================================
### E. UPDATE LEAD STATUS
### ==================================================

### E1. Update lead ID 1 — should return 200 if it belongs to org 1
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/leads/1
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "status": "qualified"
}

### E2. Invalid status — should return 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/leads/1
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "status": "pending"
}

### E3. Nonexistent lead — should return 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/leads/999999
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "status": "qualified"
}


### ==================================================
### F. DELETE LEAD
### ==================================================

### F1. Delete lead ID 1 — should return 204 if it belongs to org 1
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/leads/1
x-org-id: 1

### F2. Delete nonexistent lead — should return 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/leads/999999
x-org-id: 1


### ==================================================
### G. CROSS-TENANT ISOLATION
### ==================================================

### G1. Create a lead belonging to organization 2
# @name createOrg2Lead
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 2

{
  "name": "Organization Two Test Lead",
  "email": "org2.test@example.com",
  "company": "Organization Two"
}

### G2. Try to read organization 2's lead as organization 1
# Expected: 404, not the lead's data
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{createOrg2Lead.response.body.$.id}}
x-org-id: 1

### G3. Read the same lead as organization 2
# Expected: 200, with the lead's data
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{createOrg2Lead.response.body.$.id}}
x-org-id: 2

### G4. Try to update organization 2's lead as organization 1
# Expected: 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{createOrg2Lead.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "status": "qualified"
}

### G5. Try to delete organization 2's lead as organization 1
# Expected: 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{createOrg2Lead.response.body.$.id}}
x-org-id: 1

### G6. Confirm organization 2's lead still exists
# Expected: 200, and status should not have been changed by G4
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{createOrg2Lead.response.body.$.id}}
x-org-id: 2


### ==================================================
### H. REQUEST PARSING AND ROUTING
### ==================================================

### H1. Malformed JSON — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json
x-org-id: 1

{
  "name": "Broken JSON",
  "email": "broken@example.com",
  "company": "Test Company",

### H2. Unknown route — should return 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/this-route-does-not-exist



